---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How the pH7Builder website handles visitor data, including the browser-only blueprint and checklist tools." path="/privacy/">
  <header class="page-hero narrow-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>A small website with a small data footprint.</h1>
    <p class="lede">This site is designed to explain pH7Builder and provide useful browser-based tools without collecting the ideas you enter.</p>
  </header>
  <section class="section-tight narrow-shell prose">
    <h2>What the website does</h2>
    <p>The pH7Builder website is a static site. It does not require an account and does not include behavioural advertising or a third-party chat widget.</p>
    <h2>Blueprint generator</h2>
    <p>The blueprint generator runs in your browser. The details you enter are used to assemble the visible blueprint and starter prompt on your device. They are not submitted to pH7Builder or an AI provider.</p>
    <h2>Launch checklist</h2>
    <p>The checklist can remember progress in local browser storage. That state stays in the browser unless you copy, download or print it. You can clear it from the tool at any time.</p>
    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>Links to GitHub, Composer or other services take you to websites with their own privacy terms. pH7Builder does not control their data practices.</p>
    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>If you contact <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>, the message and address are used to respond to your enquiry and maintain the resulting business correspondence.</p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>For a privacy question about this website, email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}?subject=pH7Builder%20privacy`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
    <p><small>Last updated: 20 November 2026.</small></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
